  "claim_3": {
    "claim": "Flow Cytometry analysis of unstimulated cryopreserved PBMC from 4 subjects at weeks 0, 1 and 2 showed substantial CD4+ T-cell expression of CCR4, CCR6, CCR7 and CXCR3 in both intradermal and intramuscular groups, with no significant differences between routes.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "section": "Results",
        "quote": "The effect of vaccination route on cell trafficking was evaluated by measurement of CD4+ T cell surface expression of chemokine receptors CCR4, CCR6, CCR7 and CXCR3. This was initially performed in both mycobacteria-stimulated and unstimulated cells for 4 subjects."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "section": "Results",
        "quote": "Fig. 4D shows median expression of these chemokine markers in unstimulated cells. Substantial levels of expression were detected in both groups, which were not significantly different."
